:: Seaspray Hotel 112 Bathroom Soak
<<effects>>

<<wash>>
You filled up the bathtub with warm water then undress and soak yourself in. The warm water relaxes your mind.
<br><br>

You dry yourself, dress, and return to the room.
<br><br>

<<link [[Leave|Seaspray Hotel 112 Rest]]>><<clotheson>><</link>>


:: Seaspray Hotel 112 Clean
<<effects>>

You remove the sheets around the furniture and start to clean. Starting with the dustpan and brush for dust cleaning on the furniture, then apply a vacuum cleaner to the floor. 
<br><br>
Then finish the cleaning by using a wet rag for every nook and cranny. 
<br><br>
The room looks lived-in again. Whoever runs this place will want to know it exists.
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Seaspray Hotel 112]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Seaspray Hotel 112 Deal
<<effects>>

<<generate1>><<person1>>
You describe the room to the <<person>> at the front desk. <<He>> frowns at the ledger, taps at a keyboard, then frowns harder.
<br><br>

"One-twelve," <<he>> says, as if the number itself were an inconvenience. "That room hasn't been on the books in years. Wait here."
<br><br>

<<He>> disappears through a door behind the desk. You wait long enough to regret saying anything.
<br><br>

<<link [[Wait|Seaspray Hotel 112 Deal 2]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>


:: Seaspray Hotel 112 Deal 2
<<effects>>

<<if $hotelManager gte 1>>
    <<endevent>>
    <<loadNPC 0 "hotel_manager">><<person1>>
    The manager comes out to meet you <<himself>>, and doesn't look at all surprised to see you.
<<else>>
    <<endevent>>
    <<generate1>><<person1>>
    A <<person>> comes out in <<his>> place, carrying the ledger under one arm. <<He>> keeps the room list, apparently.
<</if>>
<br><br>

"You cleaned it," <<he>> says. It isn't a question. "Hours of work, by the look of you. And now you'd like to use it."
<br><br>

You start to explain. <<He>> raises a hand.
<br><br>

"You misunderstand. I'm not angry." <<He>> smiles, politely. "I'm quoting you a price. <<printmoney 10000>> a week, paid to this desk. No booking, no paperwork, no questions about what you do up there." <<He>> lets that sit. "Cleaning it doesn't make it yours. Paying for it does."
<br><br>

<<if $money gte 10000>>
    <<link [[Pay the first week|Seaspray Hotel 112 Deal Pay]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<<else>>
    <span class="red">You can't afford the first week.</span> <span class="blue">The desk takes cash.</span>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Turn it down|Seaspray Hotel]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Seaspray Hotel 112 Deal Pay
<<effects>>

<<set $hotel112 to 3>>
<<set $hotelRent to { stage: 1, due: Time.days + 7, arrears: 0 }>>
<<money -10000 "hotelRent">>
You hand over <<printmoney 10000>>. The <<person>> counts it, writes something in the ledger, and gives you a key on a plain ring.
<br><br>

"Same time next week," <<he>> says. "I'd hate for us to fall out over something as dull as money."
<br><br>

<i>Room 112 is yours while you keep paying. The front desk will want the week's rent every seven days.</i>
<br><br>

<<link [[Next|Seaspray Hotel]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Seaspray Hotel Rent
<!-- included by the lobby, which has already run <<effects>> -->
<<generate1>><<person1>>
The <<person>> at the front desk catches your eye as you pass, and taps the ledger with one finger.
<br><br>

<<set _hotelRentAmount to setup.hbsc.HOTEL_RENT_STAGES[Math.clamp(($hotelRent ? $hotelRent.stage : 1) - 1, 0, 4)]>><<set _hotelRentDue to _hotelRentAmount + ($hotelRent ? $hotelRent.arrears : 0)>>
<<if $hotelRent.arrears gt 0>>
    "You're behind," <<he>> says. "<<printmoney _hotelRentDue>>, including what you owe."
<<else>>
    "Room one-twelve," <<he>> says. "<<printmoney _hotelRentDue>>, when you're ready."
<</if>>
<br><br>

<<if $money gte _hotelRentDue>>
    <<link [[Pay|Seaspray Hotel Rent Pay]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<<elseif setup.hbsc.canAutoPay("hotelRent", setup.inflation.spendPrice(_hotelRentDue, "hotelRent"))>>
    <<link [[Pay from your savings|Seaspray Hotel Rent Pay]]>><</link>>
    <br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Say you'll pay later|Seaspray Hotel Rent Refuse]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Seaspray Hotel Rent Pay
<<effects>>

<<set _hotelRentAmount to setup.hbsc.HOTEL_RENT_STAGES[Math.clamp(($hotelRent ? $hotelRent.stage : 1) - 1, 0, 4)]>><<set _hotelRentDue to _hotelRentAmount + ($hotelRent ? $hotelRent.arrears : 0)>>
<<if $money gte _hotelRentDue>>
    <<money `-_hotelRentDue` "hotelRent">>
<<else>>
    <!-- the lobby only offers this branch when the standing order covers the desk's price -->
    <<run setup.hbsc.tryAutoPay("hotelRent", setup.inflation.spendPrice(_hotelRentDue, "hotelRent"))>>
<</if>>
<<set $hotelRent.arrears to 0>>
<<set $hotelRent.due to Time.days + 7>>
<<set $hotelRent.stage to Math.min($hotelRent.stage + 1, 5)>>
You pay <<printmoney _hotelRentDue>>. The <<person>> writes it down without looking up.
<br><br>

<<if $hotelRent.stage gte 2 and $hotelRent.stage lte 5>>
    "The room's worth more than it was," <<he>> adds, as you turn to go. "Next week it's <<printmoney `setup.hbsc.HOTEL_RENT_STAGES[Math.clamp($hotelRent.stage - 1, 0, 4)]`>>."
    <br><br>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Seaspray Hotel]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Seaspray Hotel Rent Refuse
<<effects>>

"Later," you say.
<br><br>

<<set _hotelRentAmount to setup.hbsc.HOTEL_RENT_STAGES[Math.clamp(($hotelRent ? $hotelRent.stage : 1) - 1, 0, 4)]>><<set _hotelRentDue to _hotelRentAmount + ($hotelRent ? $hotelRent.arrears : 0)>><<set $hotelRent.arrears += _hotelRentAmount>>
<<set $hotelRent.due to Time.days + 7>>
<<if $hotelRent.arrears gte _hotelRentAmount * 3>>
    <<set $hotel112 to 1>>
    <<unset $hotelRent>>
    <<run setup.hbsc.setAutoPay("hotelRent", false)>>
    <!-- don't strand clothes in a room the player no longer has -->
    <<storeon "Seaspray Hotel Bed" "wardrobe">>
    The <<person>> doesn't argue. <<He>> reaches under the desk, and drops a key on a plain ring into a drawer.
    <br><br>

    "Then it isn't your room," <<he>> says. "It never was. You're welcome to the lobby, like any other guest."
    <br><br>

    <span class="red">You've lost Room 112.</span> Whatever you left up there is gone, and the sheets are back over the furniture.
    <br><br>
<<else>>
    <<He>> writes something down, and underlines it. "Later," <<he>> agrees. "It goes on the tab. The tab has a limit."
    <br><br>

    <span class="red">The rent goes unpaid.</span> You can't use the room until you settle up.
    <br><br>
<</if>>

<<link [[Next|Seaspray Hotel]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


